    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AsciiDoc has basic support for bibliographies. AsciiDoc doesn’t concern itself with the structure of the bibliography entry itself, which is entirely freeform. What it does is provide a way to make references to the entries from the same document and output the bibliography with proper semantics for processing by other toolchains (such as DocBook)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To conform to output formats, a bibliography must be its own section at any level. The section must be assigned the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "bibliography"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " section style. By adding the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "bibliography"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " style to the section, you implicitly add it to each unordered list in that section."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You would define the bibliography as a level 1 section ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "=="
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") when:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "the doctype is "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "article"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "the doctype is "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "book"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " and the book doesn’t contain any parts"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "the bibliography is for a part"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "[bibliography]\n== Bibliography"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also define it as a deeper section, in which case the doctype doesn’t matter and it’s scoped to the parent section."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the book has parts, and the bibliography is for the whole book, the section is defined as a level 0 section ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "="
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "[bibliography]\n= Bibliography"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_bibliography_section_syntax",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Bibliography section syntax"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Bibliography entries are declared as items in an unordered list."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "_The Pragmatic Programmer_ <<pp>> should be required reading for all developers.\nTo learn all about design patterns, refer to the book by the \"`Gang of Four`\" <<gof>>.\n\n[bibliography]\n== References\n\n* [[[pp]]] Andy Hunt & Dave Thomas. The Pragmatic Programmer:\nFrom Journeyman to Master. Addison-Wesley. 1999.\n* [[[gof,gang]]] Erich Gamma, Richard Helm, Ralph Johnson & John Vlissides.\nDesign Patterns: Elements of Reusable Object-Oriented Software. Addison-Wesley. 1994."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Bibliography with references"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In order to reference a bibliography entry, you need to assign a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "non-numeric"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " label to the entry. To assign this label, prefix the entry with the label enclosed in a pair of triple square brackets (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "[[[label]]]"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). We call this a bibliography anchor. Using this label, you can then reference the entry from anywhere above the bibliography in the same document using the normal cross reference syntax (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<<label>>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "autowidth": false,
            "body": [
              [
                {
                  "background": null,
                  "colspan": 1,
                  "document": {
                    "blocks": [
                      {
